# Netlify redirects for the IdeaForge Software site.

# This file is copied into dist as it is. When a custom domain is set as the
# primary domain in the Netlify dashboard, the build appends one more rule below
# it, sending every request made to the .netlify.app address on to that domain
# with a 301. Removing the domain in the dashboard and redeploying drops that
# rule, and the site is served from the .netlify.app address again.

# Rules are matched from the top and the first match wins, so anything that has
# to keep answering on the .netlify.app address is listed here, ahead of it.

# Google's verification file, so the .netlify.app Search Console property stays
# verified through the move. It is forced: an unforced rule is skipped when the
# file exists, and the redirect below would win.
